From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 27 Jan 2026 16:45:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: abort ROC and mark phys resetting in full reset

mt7996_mac_full_reset() cancelled each phy's mac_work but left
remain-on-channel work pending and the phys unmarked while the
hardware went through a full reset. Abort ROC and set MT76_RESET on
every phy up front, mirroring the L1 SER recovery path; MT76_RESET
is cleared again when the phys restart.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mac.c |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -2482,8 +2482,11 @@ mt7996_mac_full_reset(struct mt7996_dev
 	ieee80211_stop_queues(hw);
 
 	cancel_work_sync(&dev->wed_rro.work);
-	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy)
+	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy) {
+		mt76_abort_roc(phy->mt76);
+		set_bit(MT76_RESET, &phy->mt76->state);
 		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&phy->mt76->mac_work);
+	}
 
 	mt76_abort_scan(&dev->mt76);
 
